{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_shggmdi2galtq6yssqcusakcltm4rdaprajjowyhxubvnok2lmta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte on every path tested. **No divergences were found; no changes to `src/lib.rs` were needed.**\n\n## What was done\n\n**Phase A** — artifacts in `translation/`:\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — all 16 C `nm -D` text symbols; Rust exports exactly the same set (0 missing, 0 extra) in both release and debug profiles. The 7 `static` C helpers correctly stay private; `stbds_unit_tests` is declared-but-never-defined in the C, so absent from both.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 50 rows: every sentinel return (`NULL`, `-1`, unchanged pointer, `temp = -1`), all 8 `STBDS_ASSERT` sites, the `min`/`max` arena constants, out-of-range `mode`/`sh_mode` enum values, and the null/zero/oversized-length boundaries.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 52 rows over the real branch axes (`mode`, `string.mode`, three map-creation routes, 9 key widths, growth/shrink/rebuild, probe path, tombstone reuse, delete position, arena block growth, the `stbds_hash_seed` global).\n\n**Phases B–D** — 76 differential tests, both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`:\n- Every map row compares the **full structural state after every single operation** — array header, entire hash index (all thresholds, `seed`, `slot_count_log2`, arena fields), every bucket's `hash[]`/`index[]`, and every element's key + value — not just return values.\n- `sh_geti` stdout compared byte-for-byte (including the `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", struct_by_value, …)` ABI quirk), with and without re-seeding.\n- Abort paths verified by forking and checking both libraries die with SIGABRT.\n- Suite passes against: release `.so`, debug `.so`, and a `-O2` C build (extra cross-check on the UB shift/signed-overflow paths).\n\n## Three notable C behaviors the tests pin down\n1. `hmdel_key` compares `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING`, not `>=` — so `mode = 2/5/1000` **aborts** when deleting a non-last element. Both libraries abort identically (`err_29`).\n2. `assert(used_count >= 0)` is tautological on `size_t`, so `used_count` wraps to `SIZE_MAX` instead of aborting (`err_14`).\n3. `stralloc`'s `512 << (block>>1)` shift is UB for `block >= 128`; both rely on the hardware's 6-bit mask and agree across all 256 `block` values (`err_17`).\n\nOne documented, deliberately-unreproduced difference: glibc's `assert` writes a message containing the C source's **build-time absolute path** to stderr before aborting; Rust calls `abort()` directly. The fatal signal matches; no other observable output differs.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (only the `build/` directory you instructed me to create)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":194,"cache_read_input_tokens":229582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":194,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"015b8b67-56ea-40c6-b01c-d271aa06b9db","uuid":"a63275ca-05d7-4249-acc0-8ac0815c6c19","timestamp":"2026-09-05T11:36:34.858Z"}
